00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:05.691
[ Laughter ]

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:07.727
Well, some TV news --
last night was yet another

00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:09.762
emotional episode
of "The Bachelorette."

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:11.496
We love that show,
and one of the --

00:07:11.496 --> 00:07:13.031
[ Applause ]
I know. It's good.

00:07:13.031 --> 00:07:14.866
One of the most memorable
moments

00:07:14.866 --> 00:07:17.936
was when Hunter and Thomas
got into a heated argument

00:07:17.936 --> 00:07:22.541
about whether Thomas was on the
show for the "right reasons."

00:07:22.541 --> 00:07:23.876
If you missed it, don't worry,

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:25.611
because here
to re-enact that scene

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:28.080
with actual lines from the show

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.050
are The Roots' own
Tariq and Questlove.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.751
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:32.751 --> 00:07:35.187 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:35.187 --> 00:07:37.255
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:37.255 --> 00:07:38.757
-Thanks, Jimmy.

00:07:38.757 --> 00:07:40.059
Tonight I'll be playing Hunter,

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:43.729
a 34-year-old single father
from Texas

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:47.266
who's concerned that Thomas
is only here for fame,

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:51.537
not to find love, like I am.

00:07:51.537 --> 00:07:53.272
-And I'll be playing Thomas,

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:55.741
a 28-year-old real-estate
broker from California

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:59.412
who doesn't feel like
he's doing anything wrong.

00:07:59.412 --> 00:08:02.181
-Very good, guys.
Whenever you're ready.

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:06.218
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:08:06.218 --> 00:08:09.121
-So, I hear the conversations
that are taking place

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.689
with you and other people,

00:08:10.689 --> 00:08:14.360
and there's this flipping and
flopping and constant smiles.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:18.297
I mean, it feels --
it feels almost like a campaign.

00:08:18.297 --> 00:08:20.699
You know?
Like you want to be Bachelor.

00:08:20.699 --> 00:08:22.969
I mean, is that something
you thought about?

00:08:22.969 --> 00:08:25.504
[ Laughter ]

00:08:25.504 --> 00:08:28.006
-I would never do anything
to hurt you,

00:08:28.006 --> 00:08:32.711
so to feel that I come
across in any way that is --

00:08:32.711 --> 00:08:34.780
This is the result --
-See?

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:39.118
See? That's the problem.
The -- I feel manipulated.

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:41.286
It just makes me really worried
about Katie

00:08:41.286 --> 00:08:43.856
because you could be
doing the same thing with her.

00:08:43.856 --> 00:08:47.659
And I would like to know --
have you ever thought

00:08:47.659 --> 00:08:50.362
maybe I could end up
being the Bachelor?

00:08:50.362 --> 00:08:53.199 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:53.199 --> 00:08:56.735
-I want to say
I appreciate you for being so --

00:08:56.735 --> 00:09:00.139
-Has being the Bachelor...

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:02.575
crossed your mind?

00:09:02.575 --> 00:09:04.610
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.146
-I...don't have
the right answer bec--

00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:09.448
-So is that your answer? Yes?

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:11.750
You are thinking about
being the Bachelor.

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:14.119
Is that what you were saying?

00:09:14.119 --> 00:09:16.155
-Uh, look,
bef-- before coming here,

00:09:16.155 --> 00:09:17.923
I didn't know what to expect.

00:09:17.923 --> 00:09:23.728
-I'm not asking
what you expected-uh!

00:09:23.728 --> 00:09:26.566
Was being the Bachelor...

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.536
Was that a prerogative for you?

00:09:30.536 --> 00:09:34.273
[ Laughter ]

00:09:34.273 --> 00:09:35.708
-Okay.

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:37.909
I can't be disingenuine
to you guys,

00:09:37.909 --> 00:09:40.012
and I'm not gonna be.

00:09:40.012 --> 00:09:42.981
So...yes.

00:09:42.981 --> 00:09:46.118
Coming into this -- this --
I had thoughts in my mind

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:48.120
that I was potentially
gonna be the --

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.721
the next Bachelor.

00:09:49.721 --> 00:09:52.458
-Like, that's messed up.

00:09:52.458 --> 00:09:55.027 line:0%
♪♪

00:09:55.027 --> 00:09:58.697
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:58.697 --> 00:10:02.034
-Touching. Thanks, guys.
Questlove and Tariq, everyone.

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:03.702
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:03.702 --> 00:10:06.672
Thank you. Gosh.
Whew. That was emotional.

00:10:06.672 --> 00:10:08.407
Wow.

00:10:08.407 --> 00:10:10.709
[ Laughter ]

00:10:10.709 --> 00:10:14.413
Some business news. Coors
