of probation and a $500 fine.

00:16:30.255 --> 00:16:31.857
Yeah, the woman said
she learned her lesson

00:16:31.857 --> 00:16:33.425
and hopes Trump pardons her

00:16:33.425 --> 00:16:36.027
when he's reinstated
as President in August.

00:16:36.027 --> 00:16:38.197
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:16:39.531 --> 00:16:42.100
Oh, my goodness.
Hey, here's some good news.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:44.836
Today after meeting with
a bipartisan group of senators,

00:16:44.836 --> 00:16:46.338
President Biden
finally announced

00:16:46.338 --> 00:16:48.907 line:0%
that they had a deal
on infrastructure.

00:16:48.907 --> 00:16:51.342 line:0%
Yeah. right now,
New Yorkers are thinking,

00:16:51.342 --> 00:16:53.512
"Okay, now, team up, and let's
save to-go cocktails.

00:16:53.512 --> 00:16:57.416
Let's go. That's the real --
Let's get to the -- Come on!"

00:16:57.416 --> 00:16:59.918
[ Applause ]

00:16:59.918 --> 00:17:02.821
That's right, Republicans and
Democrats working together --

00:17:02.821 --> 00:17:04.523
amazing.

00:17:04.523 --> 00:17:05.891
It's like one of
those YouTube videos

00:17:05.891 --> 00:17:07.592
of a lion making friends
with a squirrel.

00:17:07.592 --> 00:17:09.695
You know? It's possible.

00:17:09.695 --> 00:17:12.263
The compromise was actually
not that difficult.

00:17:12.263 --> 00:17:14.433
All it took was hard work,
determination,

00:17:14.433 --> 00:17:16.568
and a blow dart
to Mitch McConnell's neck.

00:17:16.568 --> 00:17:18.436
[ Exhales sharply, groans ]

00:17:18.436 --> 00:17:20.505
-"I've been hit."

00:17:20.505 --> 00:17:22.407
-Well, the President
held a press conference

00:17:22.407 --> 00:17:24.209
to discuss the big
infrastructure deal,

00:17:24.209 --> 00:17:26.078
which brings us to
a new piece called

00:17:26.078 --> 00:17:28.980
"Joe Biden, Whisperer-in-Chief."

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:32.518 line:0%
♪♪

00:17:32.518 --> 00:17:35.486 line:0%
-And he said, "People
are waiting for relief."

00:17:35.486 --> 00:17:41.192 line:0%
[Whispering ] I got them
$1.9 trillion of relief so far.

00:17:41.192 --> 00:17:45.830 line:0%
Just remind them, I wrote
the bill on the environment.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:48.300 line:0%
[ Normal voice ] When employers
can't find workers,

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:51.203 line:0%
I said, "Yeah [whispering]
pay them more."

00:17:51.203 --> 00:17:52.737
[ Laughter ]

00:17:52.737 --> 00:17:54.406
-What?!

00:17:54.406 --> 00:17:56.408
-I love it.

00:17:56.408 --> 00:17:58.443
-Wow.

00:17:58.443 --> 00:18:00.712
-[ Laughing ]

00:18:00.712 --> 00:18:02.447
-He closed by saying
[whispering] "If you build it,

00:18:02.447 --> 00:18:04.182
they will come."

00:18:04.182 --> 00:18:05.817
[ Laughter ]

00:18:05.817 --> 00:18:06.951
[ Normal voice ] Well,
some business news.

00:18:06.951 --> 00:18:08.954
After disappointing sales,
Dunkin' Donuts

00:18:08.954 --> 00:18:11.789
has pulled the Beyond Meat
breakfast sandwich

00:18:11.789 --> 00:18:13.291
from their national menu.

00:18:13.291 --> 00:18:14.693
-Oh, come on!

00:18:14.693 --> 00:18:17.028
-Yep. Dunkin' was shocked
plant-based foods

00:18:17.028 --> 00:18:18.897
didn't appeal to
the same customers

00:18:18.897 --> 00:18:21.533
who eat strawberry frosting
for breakfast.

00:18:21.533 --> 00:18:23.401
[ Laughter ]

00:18:23.401 --> 00:18:24.869
Some more business news.

00:18:24.869 --> 00:18:27.005
I read a headline today
that kind of confused me.

00:18:27.005 --> 00:18:31.543
It said, "T-Mobile released
its own 5G-inspired gin,"

00:18:31.543 --> 00:18:34.246
which brings us to a segment
we like to call

00:18:34.246 --> 00:18:36.114
"Uhh...I Have Some Questions."

00:18:36.114 --> 00:18:40.985
-♪ I have some questions ♪

00:18:40.985 --> 00:18:45.490 line:0%
-First up, why is a phone
company releasing its own gin?

00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:46.858 line:0%
Actually, hold on.

00:18:46.858 --> 00:18:49.861 line:0%
What does it mean
to be "5G-inspired"?

00:18:49.861 --> 00:18:53.331 line:0%
Like, does the gin
taste like a 5G network?

00:18:53.331 --> 00:18:54.900 line:0%
Wait, back up.

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:57.335 line:0%
Where would I even buy
T-Mobile gin?

00:18:57.335 --> 00:18:59.404 line:0%
Do I have to track down
a T-Mobile store,

00:18:59.404 --> 00:19:03.008 line:0%
and, if so, do they offer
unlimited gin plans?

00:19:03.008 --> 00:19:05.844 line:0%
Follow-up -- Is it cheaper
if my whole family

00:19:05.844 --> 00:19:07.946 line:0%
is on the same gin plan?

00:19:07.946 --> 00:19:10.982 line:0%
But what if my wife
doesn't like gin?

00:19:10.982 --> 00:19:13.151 line:0%
What if my kids love gin?

00:19:13.151 --> 00:19:14.686 line:0%
And again, what is
"5G-inspired"?

00:19:14.686 --> 00:19:16.255 line:0%
I just have so many questions.

00:19:17.422 --> 00:19:22.494 line:0%
-♪ I just have
so many questions ♪

00:19:22.494 --> 00:19:25.497 line:0%
-And finally, a new survey found
that nearly half of American men

00:19:25.497 --> 00:19:28.099 line:0%
experimented with their look
last year.

00:19:29.334 --> 00:19:31.335
Experimenting with your look
is one way of putting it.

00:19:31.335 --> 00:19:34.439
I mean, guys were cutting
their hair with nail clippers.

00:19:34.439 --> 00:19:35.907
Well, guys,
in a speech last night,

00:19:35.907 --> 00:19:39.644
former Vice President Mike Pence
made his clearest effort yet

00:19:39.644 --> 00:19:41.480
to distance himself from Trump

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:44.816 line:0%
by saying he was proud
to certify the election.

00:19:44.816 --> 00:19:46.752
Wow.

00:19:46.752 --> 00:19:48.754
This is a whole different side
of Pence.

00:19:48.754 --> 00:19:50.188
[ Laughter ]

00:19:50.188 --> 00:19:51.256
Next he says he wants to be

00:19:51.256 --> 00:19:52.657
grand marshal
of the pride parade.

00:19:52.657 --> 00:19:55.327
I mean, it's amazing
what's happening to him.

00:19:55.327 --> 00:19:57.662
[ Laughter ]

00:19:57.662 --> 00:20:00.565
Meanwhile, Trump can't believe
Pence turned against him.

00:20:00.565 --> 00:20:02.701
He was like, "Boy, just when
you think you know a guy

00:20:02.701 --> 00:20:05.070
that you sent an angry mob
into the Capitol building

00:20:05.070 --> 00:20:06.104
to murder."

00:20:06.104 --> 00:20:08.173
[ Laughter ]

00:20:11.176 --> 00:20:12.677
Pence also tried to
lighten the mood

00:20:12.677 --> 00:20:14.212
by telling a joke,

00:20:14.212 --> 00:20:16.614
and he delivered it
as only Mike Pence can.

00:20:16.614 --> 00:20:17.716
-There was this farmer

00:20:17.716 --> 00:20:19.017
who decided to take his cow
to market.

00:20:19.017 --> 00:20:20.852
So he loaded the cow
in the truck and the dog

00:20:20.852 --> 00:20:22.920
and headed into town.

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:24.890
But on his way there,
there was a traffic accident.

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:27.225
Cow and the truck
went in one ditch,

00:20:27.225 --> 00:20:29.294
and the farmer and the dog
went in the other.

00:20:29.294 --> 00:20:30.696
They ended up in court.

00:20:32.197 --> 00:20:35.300
And the attorney for the other
driver was questioning,

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:38.503
"Isn't it true that you said you
never felt better in your life?"

00:20:38.503 --> 00:20:40.806
He said, "Sir, would you like to
explain the circumstances

00:20:40.806 --> 00:20:41.873
in which you made that comment?"

00:20:41.873 --> 00:20:43.141
He said, "Yeah,
I reckon I would.

00:20:43.141 --> 00:20:44.409
Me and the cow
was in one ditch,

00:20:44.409 --> 00:20:46.311
and the truck and dog
was in the other.

00:20:46.311 --> 00:20:48.513
And I seen the sheriff,
and he walked over,

00:20:48.513 --> 00:20:49.847
he looked down at that dog.

00:20:49.847 --> 00:20:52.517
It had a broke back --
it wasn't going to get better.

00:20:52.517 --> 00:20:54.753
He got his revolver out and
put it next to the dog's ear,

00:20:54.753 --> 00:20:55.754
and he shot him.

00:20:55.754 --> 00:20:58.623
And again, he mercifully
put his revolver

00:20:58.623 --> 00:21:01.526
to the forehead of that cow
and pulled the trigger.

00:21:01.526 --> 00:21:04.796
Then that sheriff walked over
to me and said,

00:21:04.796 --> 00:21:05.997
'And how are you feeling?'"

00:21:05.997 --> 00:21:08.867
[ Laughter ]

00:21:08.867 --> 00:21:10.001
-Wow!

00:21:10.001 --> 00:21:12.471
-[ Laughs ]

00:21:12.471 --> 00:21:13.739
-Wow.

00:21:13.739 --> 00:21:16.007
-Wow!

00:21:16.007 --> 00:21:18.009
Then Pence was like,
"D-Darn, I told it wrong.

00:21:18.009 --> 00:21:19.577
Let me try it again
from the top.

00:21:19.577 --> 00:21:20.612
There was this farmer,

00:21:20.612 --> 00:21:23.047
he was in a ditch."

00:21:23.047 --> 00:21:24.582
What was that joke?
Seriously.

00:21:24.582 --> 00:21:26.684
If you're looking to break up
your Fourth of July barbecue,

00:21:26.684 --> 00:21:27.786
tell that one.

00:21:27.786 --> 00:21:28.854
I mean, that's --

00:21:28.854 --> 00:21:30.088
[ Laughter ]

00:21:30.088 --> 00:21:31.356
Shooting the dog?

00:21:31.356 --> 00:21:32.490
-Broken back.

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:34.359
-"Pulled his revolver out
and aimed at dog."

00:21:34.359 --> 00:21:36.627
-"He wasn't gonna get
any better."

00:21:36.627 --> 00:21:38.230
-It got worse
when the camera panned out

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:39.865
and it was just a group of
preschool kids.

00:21:39.865 --> 00:21:41.366
And they go, "Oh."

00:21:41.366 --> 00:21:43.034
Awful.

00:21:43.034 --> 00:21:45.003
[ Laughter ]

00:21:45.003 --> 00:21:47.405
Get this. According to
a new book coming out,

00:21:47.405 --> 00:21:50.308
Trump made fun, apparently,
of Rudy Giuliani

00:21:50.308 --> 00:21:51.877 line:0%
for spitting during meetings.

00:21:51.877 --> 00:21:53.145 line:0%
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:21:53.145 --> 00:21:56.148 line:0%
And even told him
that he sucked on TV.

00:21:56.148 --> 00:21:57.582
[ Laughter ]

00:21:57.582 --> 00:21:59.518
Spitting, sucking, sweating,
leaking --

00:21:59.518 --> 00:22:01.052
he's like every awful guy
at Planet Fitness

00:22:01.052 --> 00:22:02.254
rolled into one guy, you know?

00:22:02.254 --> 00:22:04.322
[ Laughter ]

00:22:04.322 --> 00:22:05.757
Rudy took it all
in stride, though.

00:22:05.757 --> 00:22:07.959
He's like, "Look, he teases me,
but at the end of the day,

00:22:07.959 --> 00:22:09.361
he also ruined my life."

00:22:09.361 --> 00:22:13.064
[ Laughter ]

00:22:13.064 --> 00:22:15.132
Meanwhile, today,
Vice President Kamala Harris

00:22:15.132 --> 00:22:18.336 line:0%
made her first visit
to the U.S./Mexico border.

00:22:18.336 --> 00:22:21.639
Yeah, she visited
the border town of El Paso.

00:22:21.639 --> 00:22:24.476
Is it me or "El Paso" is not
the best name for a border town?

00:22:24.476 --> 00:22:25.477
-Yeah.

00:22:25.477 --> 00:22:28.913
[ Laughter ]

00:22:28.913 --> 00:22:30.315
-How about No Pass-O?

00:22:30.315 --> 00:22:32.484
[ Applause ]

00:22:34.852 --> 00:22:36.187
Some business news.

00:22:36.187 --> 00:22:39.291 line:0%
Popeyes just introduced
the new "I Don't Know" meal

00:22:39.291 --> 00:22:42.661 line:0%
for people who can't decide
what to order.

00:22:43.461 --> 00:22:44.595
How can you be undecided

00:22:44.595 --> 00:22:47.532
when the entire menu
has basically one thing?

00:22:47.532 --> 00:22:49.033
[ Laughter ]

00:22:49.033 --> 00:22:50.401
It's not like
customers are thinking,

00:22:50.401 --> 00:22:53.571
"Should I have the fried
chicken or the, uh, sushi?

00:22:53.571 --> 00:22:55.239
What do you think?

00:22:55.239 --> 00:22:58.009
What do you think
I should have at Popeyes?"

00:22:58.009 --> 00:23:01.046
[ Laughter ]

00:23:03.081 --> 00:23:05.150
"How fresh are
the lobster tails?"

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:07.151
[ Laughter ]

00:23:07.151 --> 00:23:09.054
Actually, they offer
the same meal at Arby's,

00:23:09.054 --> 00:23:10.722
only it's the cook
who has no idea what's in it.

00:23:10.722 --> 00:23:11.956
-Oh, there you go.

00:23:11.956 --> 00:23:14.326
-"I don't know.
Uh, no, hey.

00:23:14.326 --> 00:23:16.260
It's bleeding, whatever it is,
so I don't know.

00:23:16.260 --> 00:23:18.763
It's something."
-"Yes, sir."

00:23:18.763 --> 00:23:20.832
-And get this, astronomers
have identified

00:23:20.832 --> 00:23:23.801
a "extremely eccentric
mini planet"

00:23:23.801 --> 00:23:25.470
that just entered
our solar system,

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:27.805
and it's on course
to pass by Earth.

00:23:27.805 --> 00:23:30.175
It's pretty exciting,
but we were curious what exactly

00:23:30.175 --> 00:23:32.811
is an extremely
eccentric mini planet?

00:23:32.811 --> 00:23:34.846
So here now
to talk about their trip

00:23:34.846 --> 00:23:37.882
is the extremely
eccentric mini planet.

00:23:37.882 --> 00:23:40.118 line:0%
♪♪

00:23:40.118 --> 00:23:42.620
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:23:42.620 --> 00:23:43.889
-[ British accent ]
Oh, my God.

00:23:43.889 --> 00:23:45.824
Jimmy, I can't believe I'm here.

00:23:45.824 --> 00:23:47.759
This is so random.

00:23:47.759 --> 00:23:49.260
[ Laughter ]

00:23:49.260 --> 00:23:51.329
-It's not too random.
We did invite you.

00:23:51.329 --> 00:23:52.864
-Totally.
It's just that astronomers

00:23:52.864 --> 00:23:54.599
are always telling me
I'm so eccentric.

00:23:54.599 --> 00:23:55.766
You know, first they'll be like,

00:23:55.766 --> 00:23:57.902
"Look at that normal planet
over there."

00:23:57.902 --> 00:24:00.538
But then I'll be like, "Um,
I'm not like the other planets.

00:24:00.538 --> 00:24:03.675
I'm a semi-amateur
craft cocktail mixologist."

00:24:03.675 --> 00:24:05.510
Hello?
-Uh-huh.

00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:09.447
So what exactly makes you
an eccentric planet?

00:24:09.447 --> 00:24:11.449
-Well, my taste in music
is super-eclectic.

00:24:11.449 --> 00:24:13.652
Like, sometimes I listen
to Lady Gaga,

00:24:13.652 --> 00:24:17.121
but then sometimes
I listen to, like, a podcast.

00:24:17.121 --> 00:24:19.524
It's like my mind
is on shuffle.

00:24:19.524 --> 00:24:21.326
[ Laughter ]

00:24:21.326 --> 00:24:23.794
-And that classifies you as an
extremely eccentric planet?

00:24:23.794 --> 00:24:25.730
-Well, technically,
it's because I'm so small.

00:24:25.730 --> 00:24:27.499
Because people --
people are always telling me

00:24:27.499 --> 00:24:29.533
"Oh my gosh, Planet,
you're so fit."

00:24:29.533 --> 00:24:33.271
And I'm like, "Um, you haven't
seen me on Taco Tuesday."

00:24:33.271 --> 00:24:35.773
[ Laughs ]

00:24:35.773 --> 00:24:38.410
-Well, maybe you could compare
and contrast yourself

00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:40.077
with another planet.
-Sure.

00:24:40.077 --> 00:24:43.081
So, like, Mars is red
and has a couple moons, right?

00:24:43.081 --> 00:24:44.582
-Sure.
-Normal planet.

00:24:44.582 --> 00:24:46.784
Whereas I collect
Funko Pop! figurines

00:24:46.784 --> 00:24:50.020
and have a mustache tattoo
on my index finger.

00:24:50.020 --> 00:24:52.657
Eccentric! Eccentric!
-Yeah, you're very eccentric.

00:24:52.657 --> 00:24:54.258
I got it. I got it.
I got it.

00:24:54.258 --> 00:24:55.627
Give me another example.

00:24:55.627 --> 00:24:59.130
-Or, like, Earth has water
and can sustain life, right?

00:24:59.130 --> 00:25:00.498
-Yeah.
-Normal planet.

00:25:00.498 --> 00:25:05.002
Whereas I perform ukulele covers
of rap songs on Periscope.

00:25:05.002 --> 00:25:07.706
Extremely eccentric.

00:25:07.706 --> 00:25:09.707
-One last thing. That's not --
[ Chuckles ]

00:25:09.707 --> 00:25:12.244
That's not --

00:25:12.244 --> 00:25:13.945
That's not your
real accent, is it?

00:25:13.945 --> 00:25:15.446
-[ American accent ]
No, it's completely fake.

00:25:15.446 --> 00:25:16.548
-All right, good.
Thank you.

00:25:16.548 --> 00:25:18.716
The extremely eccentric
mini planet.

00:25:18.716 --> 00:25:20.652
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:25:20.652 --> 00:25:22.553 line:0%
♪♪

00:25:22.553 --> 00:25:25.390
[ Laughs ] My gosh.

00:25:28.526 --> 00:25:30.228
He's a-dork-ably eccentric.

00:25:30.228 --> 00:25:31.896
-Yeah, a-dork-ably.

00:25:31.896 --> 00:25:33.365
-And finally,
earlier this week,

00:25:33.365 --> 00:25:36.000
police in Pennsylvania
broke up an exorcism

00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:38.169 line:0%
in the lumber aisle
of a Home Depot.

00:25:38.169 --> 00:25:40.205 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:25:43.841 --> 00:25:45.710
Yeah, an exorcism
in the lumber aisle.

00:25:45.710 --> 00:25:48.847
Police laughed until
the 2x4 projectile vomited.

00:25:48.847 --> 00:25:50.315
[ Laughter ]

00:25:50.315 --> 00:25:53.784
Then they held a seance to
summon a being from far beyond,

00:25:53.784 --> 00:25:55.019
a Home Depot employee.

00:25:55.019 --> 00:25:56.421
"Does anyone work here?"

